- IN PROGRESS (2026-09-02) CONSTRAINED DECODING, the tractable half of that pair. Design and the
  feasibility gate in Thesis/notes/11-evaluation-readiness.md 29-30.
  FIRST, notes 29: `schema_enforced` NEVER CONSTRAINED GENERATION. It switches
  `effective_schema_validation`, i.e. whether output is validated and repaired AFTER the fact.
  `response_format` never reaches generate() on local-gpu. Evidence: of the 350 matrix_full pairs
  where both settings used exactly one LLM call, prompt_tokens and completion_chars are identical
  350/350. The repair pass it gates runs on 2043 cases and fails on 1613 (79%). Every published
  number stands; the thesis must simply not call it schema enforcement in the generation sense.
  THE GATE REJECTED THE APPROVED LIBRARY. lm-format-enforcer does not implement `prefixItems`, and
  `Box` is `Tuple[BindingBoxData, List[int]]`, so the one unsupported construct sits at the top of
  the tree and leaves all 29 $defs beneath it unconstrained -- it admitted a string where an int
  list belongs, an invalid filter type literal, and a document missing required fields. Rewriting
  the tuple restored correctness at 57x the cost (6 char/s, could not finish a mid-sized gold query
  in 90 s). Switched to XGRAMMAR: 169/169 gold accepted, 0/8 invalid admitted, 0.04 s compile,
  ~107,000 char/s.
  `any_order=True` IS REQUIRED, NOT COSMETIC. Gold writes properties out of schema order
  (`value_filter` before `at_time`); ordered matching rejects 32/169 gold queries, a silent cap on
  19% of the testset that would have read as a finding. Asserted in tests/test_constrained_decoding.py.
  Implemented and INERT BY DEFAULT: `constrained_decoding` and `generation_token_budget` both
  default to today's behaviour; configs/eval_config.json still dry-runs to 8112 planned runs with
  the grammar off. Three rungs (D0 free/2000, D1 free/4000, D2 constrained/4000) because TRUNCATION
  and SCHEMA VIOLATION are separate mechanisms -- failed generations run median 794 completion
  tokens against 357 and pile up at the 2000 cap -- and without D1 they are confounded.
  PRE-REGISTERED: the oracle caps this at 0.6099 against a floor of 0.7250, so CLEARING THE FLOOR
  IS NOT ON THE TABLE. If schema_valid_rate at D2 is not ~1.0 the constraint is not binding and
  nothing downstream is readable.
  NEXT, needs the cluster:
    1. bash scripts/make_eval_env.sh   (adds xgrammar; its guard must report nothing moved)
    2. sbatch --array=0-2 slurm/submit_decoding_ablation.sh   with --limit 2 first, as a smoke
    3. the smoke is a REAL GATE: confirm xgrammar works against transformers 5.5.0 (untested
       locally -- local is 4.57.1), that schema_valid_rate at D2 is ~1.0, and that the per-token
       overhead leaves 169 cases inside the 14 h limit. If overhead > ~3x, revisit before the run.

