- DONE (2026-09-22, notes 43.2: fixed before the agentic runs -- today's commits had already moved
  pipeline_fingerprint, so the reason to wait was gone; old runs rescored with --recompute; the
  TOLERANT variant was NOT adopted, a tree with broken edges keeps scoring structural 0)
  (was OPEN, DECISION 2026-09-21) tag_testset_bb._longest_path measures depth from node 0, not from the
  structural root, so a tree whose root is not node 0 loses its T5 label. Found while validating dev-set
  entry 20 (a four-box container chain rooted at node 3), which should carry T5 and carries no T-label
  at all. The bug can only ever produce FALSE NEGATIVES on T5: depth(0) walks a subpath of the real
  root's path, so it can understate the depth but never overstate it. T5 is the only label affected --
  T1/T2/T3 read the node count and T4 reads per-node children, both root-independent.
  MEASURED BEFORE DECIDING (scratchpad, stubs; the minimal patch is depth(root_node_index(query)),
  everything else in the function byte-identical):
    * GOLD IS UNAFFECTED. 3 of 169 testset entries have a non-zero root (35, 36, 135), and all three
      have exactly 3 nodes, so they cannot reach T5 under either version. data/testset_bb_labels.json,
      the per-BB slices and the coverage floors do not move, and tag_testset_bb.py need not be re-run
      over the testset.
    * PREDICTIONS BARELY MOVE. matrix_v2/merged: 20 of 8112 predictions have a non-zero root, 1 record
      changes, structural_f1 0.3245 -> 0.3245 (+0.0000). matrix_full: 23 off-root, 3 records change,
      0.3216 -> 0.3217 (+0.0001). Both are two orders of magnitude below the +-0.03 resolution of
      notes 37.7, so no published number changes.
    * NO LLM RE-RUN IS NEEDED IF IT IS FIXED. _recompute_metrics re-derives metrics.structural from
      each record's own gold_query and prediction via _structural_metrics -> detect_bb_labels, with no
      GPU and no ocpq_cli; that is what the result store is for. matrix_v2/merged and matrix_full both
      have a result_store. non_oracle does NOT (per-shard stores only), so it would be recomputed
      shard by shard.
    * COST OF FIXING: tag_testset_bb.py is in _PIPELINE_SOURCE_FILES, so pipeline_fingerprint moves and
      no future shard matches the existing matrix. That is already true post-reorg (notes 38), but it
      means the fix must not land between shards of one matrix.
  RECOMMENDATION: fix it AFTER the agentic runs, not during them, and recompute rather than re-run.
  CLAUDE.md forbids refactoring working code mid-experiment, and a +0.0001 correction does not justify
  moving the fingerprint while the agentic arm is being measured against the existing arms.
  SEPARATE AND LARGER, FOUND THE SAME WAY, NOT YET A DECISION: a tolerant _longest_path -- one that
  skips edges to non-existent nodes and guards against cycles instead of raising -- moves structural_f1
  by +0.0176 on matrix_v2 and changes 544 records. Today a malformed prediction whose edges cycle or
