- DONE (2026-09-22) OCPQ PROVENANCE IS RECORDED IN EVERY RUN. QueryExecutor.ocpq_provenance()
  writes config_resolved.json["ocpq"] = {rev, branch, dirty, dirty_files, binaries: {ocpq_cli,
  ocpq-web-server}: {path, sha256, bytes, mtime}, cli_older_than_source, cli_mode, build_error}.
  summary.json gets ocpq_cli_sha256 and ocpq_cli_changed_during_run (re-hashed at the end: array
  tasks share one checkout, so another job's rebuild would otherwise split a run between two
  evaluators). --merge-shards reports ocpq_consistent (True / False / None = a shard predates
  this) and ocpq_cli_sha256s. Recorded, never a gate -- it warns loudly on a dirty checkout, a
  stale binary, a failed build or a missing binary. Never raises. tests/test_ocpq_provenance.py
  (21 checks, a real throwaway git checkout); it caught a real bug on the way (stdout.strip() ate
  the leading space of `git status --porcelain`, truncating the first dirty filename).
  WHY build=True: ocpq_cli runs through `cargo run --release`, which REBUILDS the binary whenever
  the OCPQ source is newer than it. Hashing first would record the binary cargo is about to
  replace. So the run triggers the build (the existing _detect_cli_mode call, which every run
  already made on its first query) and hashes afterwards. Only the timing of that build moves.
  TWO CORRECTIONS TO MY OWN EARLIER STATEMENTS, found doing this:
    * The live evaluator was NOT the "3 April binary". The workspace root is OCPQ/, so cargo
      runs OCPQ/target/release/ocpq_cli.exe, built 2026-08-28 (sha256 192522ea...). The 3 April
      file is OCPQ/backend/target/release/ocpq_cli.exe, a stale leftover nothing runs.
    * Restoring the two modified files on 2026-09-21 made them newer than that binary, so the
      next local `cargo run` would have rebuilt the evaluator silently. HEAD was 2c5e0d6 from
      2026-08-18 to 2026-09-21, so the 08-28 binary and the pinned 50f60c1 share their ocpq_cli
      source; a rebuild should be equivalent, but equivalent is a claim, so it was tested (below).
  REBUILT 2026-09-22 from nlxocpq-pinned 50f60c1: ocpq_cli sha256 0f2ff455..., same size, new
  hash (Rust builds are not bit-reproducible). EQUIVALENCE VERIFIED: every gold query of the
  testset, run through QueryExecutor.run_ocpq_query on the rebuilt binary, reproduces the root
  situation set the previous binary stored in eval_runs/_discriminability_store on 2026-09-02 --
