- OPEN, DESIGN (2026-09-22, user-approved: A3 as a SEPARATE rung) A3 = A1 + A FROZEN LESSON MEMORY
  BUILT ON THE DEV SET. Origin: over a long session of hand-modelling queries the assistant got
  steadily better, and the transferable part of that was accumulated LESSONS (SAT/AND pass
  vacuously on an empty child; only the root box is scored; declared-type traps; O2O qualifiers),
  not an accumulated transcript. The models reset per case today -- _run_pipeline_agentic builds a
  fresh message list every case -- and that is correct for A0-A2.
  WHY NOT CHAIN THE TESTSET CASES: (1) case 80 would learn from cases 1-79, which is a different,
  online protocol and no longer comparable to the one-shot arms; (2) the score would depend on case
  ORDER and on where --case-shard splits, and every shard starts empty; (3) the agent has no
  correctness signal on the testset -- only probe counts -- so carried lessons harden right or
  wrong alike; (4) a 15-turn case already fills much of a small model's usable window
  (PromptTooLongError ends the loop), so raw cross-case history overflows within a few cases.
  THE DESIGN: run the agent over data/agent_devset.json (38 entries, NEVER scored in the thesis, so
  its gold is legitimately usable -- the same standing as training data), show it its score and the
  gold after each entry, and have IT write short lessons. Distil to a cap (~1-1.5k tokens, so small
  models can hold it), FREEZE and hash into the manifest before any scored run, and inject into
  every testset case as prompt text. Cases stay independent: order stops mattering and sharding
  stays safe.
  CONSTRAINTS: the MODEL writes the lessons, not us -- human-written lessons (our dev-set notes)
  are expertise injected into the prompt, a separate "expert notes" ablation, never system
  performance. The lessons may never be tuned on testset results, same freeze rule as the prompt.
  ATTRIBUTION: A3 - A1 is learning-from-experience; keep A2 - A1 as budget alone, so A2 stays
  budget-only and does NOT get the memory.
  THE UNLEASHED ARM: if an "anything goes" number is wanted (the supervisor's second evaluation),
  make it A4 = tools + large budget + memory, and report it as a SYSTEM CEILING whose components
  are already decomposed by A1/A2/A3 -- not as an attributable effect. Budget-gated, like the
  frontier arm.
  COST: one extra pass over 38 dev entries per model, then the same 169 cases as A1.

- OPEN, DESIGN (2026-09-22) IS "THINKING" A MATRIX VARIABLE FOR THE AGENTIC ARM? Raised because
  Claude Code reasons before acting and several evaluated models have no reasoning mode.
  THE BLOCKER, checked in the code: the agentic loop constrains EVERY turn to AgentAction
  (LLM._run_pipeline_agentic) and the xgrammar processor is attached whenever constrained_decoding
  is on (LLM._ocpq_logits_processor, :1561). A native reasoning model therefore CANNOT emit its
  thinking tokens under our protocol -- the grammar masks everything that is not the action JSON.
  With constrained decoding off it could, but _parse_agent_action takes the first `{`, so a think
  block containing braces becomes a malformed action. Native reasoning is thus not a clean
  crossable factor: it is available to some models only, and it fights the protocol.
  PROPOSAL: make reasoning a PROTOCOL-LEVEL variable instead -- add an optional `thought: str` to
  AgentAction and a line to AGENT_PROTOCOL_RULES. Every model can then reason, inside the grammar,
  whether or not it has a native mode, and the variable is crossable and comparable. It is the
  agentic analogue of schema-chain-of-thought-plus in the non-agentic matrix.
  SCOPE, because every binary factor DOUBLES the GPU cells: cross `thought` on the tool rung A1
  only (2 cells per model), not on every rung. Measure it first on the dev set in the Stage 4 model
  gate -- malformed-action rate, turns used, tool calls -- before spending matrix time; a model
  that cannot hold the protocol WITH a thought field is a finding on its own.
  CAVEATS to record: a thought costs tokens every turn, so A1-with-thought and A1-without must
  share the same turn budget and case_timeout_sec, and the comparison then includes that cost.
  Native reasoning modes (if any evaluated model has one) stay a separate, model-specific arm,
  reported apart and never as a matrix cell.

